## 9. Privacy center

```
┌──────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Sidebar              │ Privacy                                                   │
│                      │ Overview · Sent to Meta · Retention · Exclusions · Delete │
│                      │                                                           │
│                      │ ON THIS MAC                                   2.3 GB      │
│                      │  Screenshots (redacted)   6 days · 4,112      1.9 GB      │
│                      │  Activity events          30 days             210 MB      │
│                      │  Discoveries & steps      until dismissed      12 MB      │
│                      │  Automations & builds     until deleted       160 MB      │
│                      │  Encrypted at rest · FileVault on ✓                       │
│                      │                                                           │
│                      │ SENT TO META (last 30 days)            [ View all → ]     │
│                      │  41 requests · 38 text-only · 3 with screenshots · $4.12  │
│                      │                                                           │
│                      │ Local-only mode  [ off ]  Keep observing, send nothing.   │
│                      │  Discoveries become less accurate; builds are paused.     │
└──────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### 9.1 Sent to Meta (per-request log)

Every model call (pattern analysis, build turns, repairs, key tests) is logged locally
**before** it is sent, with its exact payload. The log is the evidence that the privacy copy
is true.

```
 Sent to Meta                                  Filter: [All purposes ▾] [30 days ▾]
 ┌──────────┬──────────────────────┬────────────────┬───────────────┬────────┐
 │ When     │ Purpose              │ Model          │ Contents      │ Cost   │
 ├──────────┼──────────────────────┼────────────────┼───────────────┼────────┤
 │ 10:41    │ Build: Weekly status │ muse-wonder-1.0│ 4.2k tok text │ $0.06  │
 │ 10:39    │ Build: Weekly status │ muse-wonder-1.0│ text + 3 imgs │ $0.21  │
 │ 03:00    │ Nightly pattern pass │ muse-spark-1.3 │ 11k tok text  │ $0.03  │
 └──────────┴──────────────────────┴────────────────┴───────────────┴────────┘
 Select a row → payload viewer:
 ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
 │ Request 10:39:12 · Build: Weekly status CSV · api: Meta (via Muse)        │
 │ Text (redactions highlighted)            │ Images (3)                      │
 │ "Step 2: Copy Key, Summary, Status from  │ ┌────┐ ┌────┐ ┌────┐           │
 │  ticket ▇▇▇ (name) …"                    │ │▇ ▇ │ │▦▦▦ │ │▇▇  │           │
 │                                          │ └────┘ └────┘ └────┘           │
 │ [ Copy as JSON ]   [ This contains something private → add a rule ]       │
 └───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

**Hard dependency for tracks 04/12:** the build path goes through Muse, and Muse makes its own
requests (tool results, file contents, web fetches). Macroscope can log what *it* hands to Muse
directly. Logging every provider request Muse makes needs either Muse's own session
records (`session/read`, item stream) or a local proxy on `--base-url`. **[assumption]** The
UI copy has to match whichever is achievable. If only Macroscope-side inputs can be logged,
the header says "Sent to Muse for builds" and explains that Muse's internal requests include
the files in the build folder.

### 9.2 Retention

Separate sliders for each data class, because the classes differ a lot in sensitivity:

```
 Screenshots       1 day ●──────────── 30 days     now: 7 days
 Activity events   7 days ──────●───── 90 days     now: 30 days
 Sent-to-Meta log  kept as long as events (it's metadata about your data)
```

Lowering a slider shows "This will delete 3,120 screenshots now", and the change takes effect
after a 5 s undo window.

### 9.3 Exclusions

One list with three rule kinds: **Apps**, **Websites** (domain, with category packs), and
**Window titles containing…** (e.g. "Confidential", "HR -"). There is also **Schedule** (e.g.
never observe outside 8:00–19:00 or on weekends). Every rule shows its origin ("added from
onboarding", "added from 'Never suggest for Jira'", "added from payload viewer"), so users can
see how their own clicks shaped the rules.

### 9.4 Delete

```
 Delete captured data
 [ Last hour ]  [ Today ]  [ Choose range… ]          Undo available for 10 s
 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 Delete everything Macroscope has captured
 Screenshots, events, discoveries and the request log. Your automations
 stay (they're yours) unless you also check:  ☐ Delete automations too
 This can't be undone.                      [ Delete everything… ]  (red)
```

"Delete everything" is the one place a typed confirmation is justified ("type DELETE"),
because it is truly irreversible and rare. Data Meta already received can't be recalled by
the app, and the sheet says so, pointing at Meta's data policy **[assumption: Meta API
retention terms not verified; track 03/08 to confirm]**.

