plan/research/09-pattern-engine.md:133:## 3. Episodes, actions, and task continuity
plan/research/09-pattern-engine.md:137:[assumption] Hard-close episodes on lock, pause, sleep, permission loss, or 120 seconds idle. An app/window/tab switch starts a provisional segment. Continue the episode when the previous context returns within 45 seconds, a clipboard edge crosses the switch, or a known document/file relation connects it. Otherwise close at the switch after 45 seconds of unrelated activity. Use a 30-minute episode cap with continuation links. These boundaries have explicit reasons and confidence; they are revisable. Ambiguous segments remain separate, with candidate mining permitted across adjacent segments only when a dataflow or high-confidence task link exists. Never bridge privacy gaps.
plan/research/09-pattern-engine.md:150:[assumption] Collapse focus-click-focus into one activation; combine shortcut plus clipboard notification into one copy; combine paste plus field focus into one paste. Preserve undo/retry as annotations rather than silently removing them. Clipboard hash/generation match plus timing and focused target supports a transfer edge; mere Cmd+V supports `paste_attempt`. Retain observed and inferred actions distinctly. Never infer cell B2 from screen coordinates alone.
plan/research/09-pattern-engine.md:171:## 4. Discover repetition locally
plan/research/09-pattern-engine.md:181:[assumption] Weekly periodicity uses local weekday/time-of-day histograms with 30-minute bins and +/-60-minute tolerance. Label “usually Tuesdays around 2pm” only after four observed weeks, >=75% matching weeks, and concentration above the user's overall activity baseline. Track recording coverage: an unobserved Tuesday is unknown, not a missed workflow. Preserve original timezone and handle DST in local time. Multiple jobs in a Tuesday batch count as one schedule occurrence. A schedule raises explanatory relevance, never establishes repetition or automatically creates a trigger.
plan/research/09-pattern-engine.md:185:## 5. Friction, feasibility, and ranking
plan/research/09-pattern-engine.md:192:e = min(undo_or_retry_annotations / eligible_actions, 0.25)
plan/research/09-pattern-engine.md:198:[assumption] Undo and retries are friction proxies, not proven mistakes. Count an undo followed by re-entry to the same field within ten seconds once; do not label ordinary undo as user error. Cap multipliers to prevent noisy capture dominating ranking. Show `F*D` as observed weekly effort; Friction is a ranking unit, never minutes saved.
plan/research/09-pattern-engine.md:213:[assumption] Support strength starts at 0.6 for three executions and reaches 1 at eight executions across three dates; cap at 0.7 for a single-day batch. Offer buildable suggestions only with complete essential-step coverage, `A>=0.60`, `Q>=0.65`, and estimated savings >=10 minutes/week, or a batch saving >=5 minutes. Schedule-specific suggestions additionally require the periodicity threshold. Unavailable capability evidence yields an internal candidate or “teach this workflow” state, never an “Automate this” promise. Prefer automating a verified subset, such as producing an import CSV, when the full write path is unsupported.
plan/research/09-pattern-engine.md:217:## 6. Meta inference: bounded explanation jobs
plan/research/09-pattern-engine.md:223:[assumption] Default nightly execution occurs at the next idle/unlocked opportunity after 02:00, on power when possible. No LLM per click or per frame. Explain at most five new/materially changed clusters per day, with one request per cluster; cache by sanitized packet hash plus model/prompt version. Near-real-time means local scoring when an episode closes. A model request occurs early only when the user opens an unexplained candidate and explicitly requests its explanation, using the same daily budget.
plan/research/09-pattern-engine.md:225:[assumption] Per-cluster packet: task-neutral instruction and output schema; metrics; supported capability IDs; one medoid and two contrasting occurrences, up to 60 actions each; observed field/type mappings; missing evidence; up to three cropped redacted keyframes illustrating source, destination, and result. Images are omitted by default and added only when text evidence cannot resolve ambiguity and the user has enabled image sharing. Recheck redaction at egress; drop unsafe artifacts. Use request-local aliases and relative times, omit document tokens and full OCR dumps. Treat all OCR, labels, and previews as quoted untrusted evidence.
plan/research/09-pattern-engine.md:227:[assumption] Reserve <=4,000 text input tokens and <=1,000 visible output tokens/job; daily text ceiling 20,000 input and 5,000 output, plus a separately metered image allowance <=six crops/day. Downsample crops to 768 pixels on the long edge; actual image token accounting and hidden reasoning costs are unknown until a successful call. These are application admission budgets, not a claim that the CLI enforces token maxima. Set low reasoning and one model step; reserve conservatively, reconcile provider usage, and stop admitting calls on quota/cost exhaustion. Until pricing and image metering are verified, disable image jobs and use a conservative owner-configurable monetary ceiling; one in-flight call may exceed a soft estimate. Budget failure leaves deterministic suggestions available.
