89:### 1.3 MVP in/out
91:The private MVP includes signed Mac installation; sample, Tell, and bounded native Show; an editable Task Contract; local fixture import; explicit Meta key setup; text-first analysis; MSP build transcript; key-free terminal drawer; SDK transforms and brokered file/clipboard effects; host-owned tests; preview and approval; manual/hotkey pinning; receipts, undo, rollback, and one-click reviewed repair. All privacy ship blockers in section 8 are included.
93:Keep these out: ambient capture, spontaneous discovery notifications, browser control, network-enabled tools, runtime LLM nodes, folder auto-runs, schedules, OAuth, native form filling, arbitrary script execution, Python, custom generated UI, billing/accounts, sync, sharing, gallery, teams, and mobile. Do not add the filesystem watcher just because it appears easy: unattended trigger semantics require trust, readiness, deduplication, and recovery.
