562:### 4.5 API-key authentication: verified versus unverified
566:| Finding | Status | Consequence |
568:| Bogus `META_API_KEY` reaches Meta from `muse serve` | VERIFIED-local, probes A/B | Serve reads the child environment; that brief-level uncertainty is closed |
569:| Warm real-home failure arrives at `turn/completed.error.kind=authRequired` | VERIFIED-local | Observe turn terminal, not just RPC result or stderr |
570:| Fresh isolated home can return empty bundled catalog and misleading “not logged in” | VERIFIED-local | Do not tell users to consumer-login; classify initialization diagnostics separately |
571:| `exec --api-key-stdin` is the same key lane | VERIFIED-local, D–G | Use stdin for exec, reserving serve stdin for MSP |
572:| Fresh-home exec may exit before any JSONL | VERIFIED-local | Capture exit and scrubbed stderr as well as stdout |
573:| Fake exec endpoint sees Bearer credential on catalog GET | VERIFIED-local, G | Stdin avoids argv exposure but does not change provider authentication |
574:| Shared account mutation clobbered personal credential | VERIFIED-local, section 0.3 | Never call `account/*`, login/logout, or auth-set from Macroscope |
576:| Serve honors `--base-url` | Refuted locally | Do not propose an implemented key-injecting proxy for serve |
577:| Successful real-key turn, invoice attribution, usage totals, reminder costs | UNVERIFIED | Must pass M0/M1 before paid generation is offered |
578:| Live approvals, quota behavior, Windows credential/sandbox path | Schema/docs only, UNVERIFIED-runtime | Exercise explicitly before platform release |
