666:### 5.4 Windows design and verification
672:Official Muse docs now publish Windows installation and platform support, resolving the absence-of-installer assumption in reports 04/12. [VERIFIED-docs: [Muse Code platform support](https://dev.meta.ai/docs/muse-code).] This does not establish successful Windows MSP, sandbox, XDG isolation, ConPTY, or package integration. Do not ship a “lite” homegrown general agent merely because those tests are pending.
674:Use hosted CI for compile/replay/schema/package checks; an agent-operated interactive Windows environment for picker, UIA, OCR, consent, update and cancellation; and an independent physical x64 tester for GPU, border, DPI, sleep/wake, Defender, and SmartScreen. The owner can inspect recorded synthetic test artifacts from Mac. If no tester is funded, Windows remains an explicitly incomplete preview. ARM64 is a later separately tested target.
