809:### 7.3 Runtime and effect protocol
817:Use replay (fixture reads, simulated effects), plan (selected real reads, staged effects), and live (authorized effects). Approve the exact plan hash plus input/output preconditions; changed inputs or targets force replanning. Plan cannot guarantee later live results. Start one active run/tool and two globally; cancel entire process groups/Job Objects. Timeout or denial pauses that tool and disables its queued triggers.
819:### 7.4 Tests, undo, trust, and repair
829:Classify failures before repair: auth→replace key; quota/network→bounded wait; input validation→choose/correct mapping; permission→review grant; code/data drift→prepare repair. Repair uses a new branch/workspace/session, a reviewed synthetic packet, and a host-owned regression reproducing the fault. At most two repair candidates; original and new tests must pass, permissions cannot widen, and the user approves the new version. No automatic patch deployment or uncertain-effect replay. Rollback selects an earlier valid signed version; it does not undo effects already committed.
831:## 8. Privacy and security
833:### 8.1 Threat model and non-promises
839:### 8.2 Prompt-injection defenses
851:### 8.3 MUST-for-MVP ship blockers
853:| ID | Required implementation/evidence |
855:| P1 | No raw pixels/OCR/AX content on disk, IPC, logs, or crash attachments; sanitize before persistence and egress; fail closed on detector failure. |
856:| P2 | Allowlisted scope, secure-field/lock/pause gating, visible capture state, barrier race tests, browser exclusion without heuristics fallback. |
857:| P3 | SQLCipher metadata/shards, authenticated encrypted blobs/fixtures/preimages, device-vault keys, no plaintext temporary files or fallback. |
858:| P4 | Images 24 h, detail 7 d, aggregates 30 d; lineage-aware app/range/wipe deletion; queued-job cancellation and backup exclusions. |
859:| P5 | Separate egress consent, payload preview, exact direct-request log, honest Muse-input log, local-only admission stop, Contributor ban. |
860:| P6 | Own credential item; no shared Muse auth mutation; no key in argv/prompts/PTY/runtime; successful API-billing and rejected-key tests. |
861:| P7 | No arbitrary keyed shell; proved Muse tool/read containment or zero-tool fallback; generated runtime has no model key. |
