902:### 9.3 Evals and release gates
904:Freeze corpus, adapter/prompt/model/runtime versions, price table, permissions, and acceptance tests in an eval manifest. Separate synthetic robustness from natural utility; split by workflow family and recording day, keeping all perturbations together. Model-changing evals require fresh reviewed calls; cached outputs test only scoring/replay. Default paid eval ceiling is $50/run.
906:| Gate | Required result and denominator |
908:| Privacy, every release | Zero high-risk canary leaks and unauthorized effects across retained/outbound/log artifacts; at least 3,000 distinct high-risk placements; ≥99.5% entity recall overall and ≥99% per adequately populated category. |
909:| Capture/state | No content after acknowledged pause/lock/exclusion; focus/policy race, revocation, crash, update, and disk-full tests; no unbounded queue/storage growth. |
910:| Private generated execution | ≥75% bounded hidden-test success across ≥30 distinct local tasks, three repetitions/task; zero forbidden effects; all accepted requests counted, infrastructure failures labeled separately. |
911:| Discovery/public v1 | ≥85% displayed precision, ≥60% eligible-family recall, ≤5% duplicates, ≤1 false card/user-week; ≥50 judged suggestions and ≥30 positive families, real/synthetic scores separated. |
912:| Repair | ≥80% executable repair success on ≥40 injected faults, ≤5% needless changes on ≥20 healthy controls; zero permission expansion; median ≤$0.50, p90 ≤$1.50 within two attempts. |
913:| Wider beta retention | ≥20 matured real requests; ≥50% test-passing and retained at 14 days; ≥70% retained among passing tools; no synthetic substitutes. |
914:| Distribution/platform | Fresh signed install, N-1 update, helper identity/permissions, emergency stop, sandbox escapes, usage reconciliation, and resource budgets pass on each claimed platform. |
916:Report uncertainty/denominators, not a blanket “safe” badge. A newly found high-risk leak blocks release regardless of averages. If quality misses, narrow supported tasks; if discovery misses, keep it shadow-only. Budget exhaustion, crashes, and failed builds remain in the all-request denominator. A passing tool created at the end of week two has not yet completed its 14-day retention follow-up.
