+# Plan review dispositions
+
+Revised 23 October 2026 against [BRIEF](../BRIEF.md), [PLAN](../PLAN.md), and [codex-review](codex-review.md). All ten ranked findings are accepted. The table also covers the review's additional spike, UX, and preservation recommendations. Acceptance specifies future implementation/evidence requirements; it does **not** mean a gate has passed. No paid calls, credential operations, permission changes, or probe reruns were performed. Only PLAN.md and this file were changed; historical research/probes remain evidence, including their unsafe or superseded recommendations.
+
+| Review point | Accepted or rejected | What changed or why rejected |
+|---|---|---|
+| **1a. Probe 21 is an unacknowledged startup failure, not successful API-key inference** | Accepted | PLAN §§0, 4.3, 4.5 now record unavailable `:auto-review`, `permission_profile_reviewer_unavailable`, rejected session start, and no turn. Checked [21-goodkey.jsonl](../probes/transcripts/21-goodkey.jsonl) against [probe client](../probes/msp_probe.py): empty environment overrides plus inherited-key removal cannot establish the app-key lane. The older README index omits this artifact. |
+| **1b. Historical real-key command/harness is unsafe** | Accepted | §4.5 explicitly supersedes research 04 §0.2's secret-bearing `--env` command. Requires a dedicated secure-input/private-pipe harness, allowlisted environment, scrub-before-write bounded logs, deny-by-default approvals without first-choice fallback, deadlines/reaping, and exact RPC/session/acknowledged-turn matching. Verified argv exposure, automatic approval, raw logging, and broad terminal predicate in [research 04](../research/04-muse-msp.md#02-successful-call-with-a-real-key-not-run) and [msp_probe.py](../probes/msp_probe.py). No harness implementation is claimed. |
+| **1c. Approval mode is not permission profile; prove a usable posture** | Accepted | §4.3 and M0 require reproducing/classifying startup failure, selecting an actually supported available profile, recording effective policy, and separately testing `promptUnmatched`. Checked [SessionStartParams](../reference/msp/msp.d.ts): `permissionProfile` and `approvalMode` are distinct; a comment mentioning profile-list discovery does not establish a typed callable method. No invented config or global configuration change. |
+| **1d. Prove paid identity and native Muse containment; use fallback promptly** | Accepted | §§4.3–4.5 require fresh HOME/XDG + dedicated app key + explicit Standard model + exact successful turn/usage + API-dashboard attribution, and warm-personal-session/rejected-app-key control. Shell-only help is not native-read/web/plugin/child/reviewer confinement. Checked [serve help](../reference/muse-cli-help.txt), [probe 18](../probes/transcripts/18-env-leak-usershell.jsonl), and [research 04](../research/04-muse-msp.md). Failed posture/confinement immediately selects the direct zero-tool Meta path; M0 UI work cannot outrun that decision. |
+| **1e. Responses structured-output nesting and live fixture** | Accepted | §§4.1 and 10 specify `POST /v1/responses` with `text.format`, not top-level `response_format`, plus frozen successful synthetic request/response, schema validation, output limit/truncation/refusal/auth/quota/error fixtures and usage. Confirmed the distinction in [Meta Responses compatibility notes](https://dev.meta.ai/docs/protocols/responses). Live compatibility remains open. |
+| **2a. Deno and outer confinement are unproved; pin one launch before SDK work** | Accepted | §7.3 now selects a signed launcher/Seatbelt-wrapper experiment rather than an open-ended sequence of sandbox projects. Requires actual version/digest/argv/env/profile/entitlements/limits/denial artifacts before generated execution outside synthetic developer work. No unsupported pin or tested boundary is invented. Failed launch/limits narrows to finite host-owned CSV mapping, with no embedded expressions; WASI stays later research. Checked the unverified flags/JIT assumptions in [research 10 §§4.1–4.4](../research/10-microapp-runtime.md). |
+| **2b. Module-loader and storage/resource traps** | Accepted | §7.3 requires full canonical immutable import-graph allowlisting under the OS boundary during validation and execution; rejects external file/remote/data/blob imports, symlinks, hidden-fixture imports, packages/native addons, dynamic imports and generated config/hooks. Adds loader/cache/worker attacks and aggregate process-tree CPU/memory/output/scratch/cache bounds; heap flags alone do not pass. Verified the documented exceptions in [Deno security](https://docs.deno.com/runtime/fundamentals/security/) and [permissions](https://docs.deno.com/runtime/reference/permissions/). Hidden oracles stay outside worker read/import access (§7.4). |
+| **3. Approval must bind the bytes committed** | Accepted | §§2.6, 2.8, 7.3 and P8 replace generated replay/plan/live execution with stage once → compare → trusted commit. Worker exits before approval; broker commits those exact staged digests without a generated-code rerun. Defines canonical plan binding version/runtime/SDK/dependencies, inputs, native destination identity/name, ordered effects, byte lengths/digests, limits and grant/policy revisions; rechecks handles/preconditions and atomic no-overwrite publication. Adds differing-output/tamper/swap/revocation/crash fixtures. Later rename batches need frozen mappings and partial-failure recovery. |
+| **4. Preview/transcript/HTML/terminal UI can bypass runtime isolation** | Accepted | Added §8.4 and P11: escape untrusted text, disable raw Markdown HTML/remote images, sanitize necessary markup, host-render forms/invoices, isolate HTML with zero Tauri IPC and restrictive CSP, deny scripts/resources/navigation/popups/downloads, and require safe external HTML documents. Adds malicious CSV/label/source/diff/transcript/HTML/terminal fixtures. Restores safeguards from [research 05 §2](../research/05-alt-builders.md#2-muse-tui-in-an-embedded-pty) and [research 11 §6](../research/11-architecture-codex.md); checked [Tauri capabilities](https://v2.tauri.app/reference/acl/capability/). Terminal clipboard/URL controls remain mandatory when that deferred feature enters. |
+| **5. Local-only and deletion need an active-work acknowledgment barrier** | Accepted | §§2.7, 3.1–3.3, 4.5, P4/P5 and evals now define durable egress states/epochs, dispatch revocation, queue cancellation, direct-transport cancellation, keyed host/descendant termination and reaping, and unknown-charge reconciliation before acknowledgment. Deletion tombstones lineage first, cancels affected work, and removes/rekeys pending packets, fixtures, sessions, staging, undo, outbound/log material. Recovery cannot redispatch revoked input. Distinguishes Pause observation, Stop build/tools, Local-only and Delete; already-transmitted provider work cannot be recalled. |
+| **6. Private MVP and two-week schedule contain too many systems** | Accepted | §§0–3, 8–10 and owner defaults now freeze one Tell-first, selected-CSV → create-only CSV path, host comparison, immutable versions, save/manual second-input run and receipts. Defers capture/storage, terminal, clipboard/hotkey, moves, invoice/report families, general undo, full repair, discovery and browser companion. Detailed later designs remain, with feature-specific gates. M0 is evidence; M1–M4 are capacity hypotheses to re-estimate from actual engineering/support effort. |
+| **7. Observer does not supply assumed action/dataflow signals** | Accepted | Added §6.1 provenance matrix covering native focus/window state, AX/UIA state notifications, frame/OCR state, gaps, deliberate corrections, app-owned picker/broker events and later extension events. Third-party export/download/mapping/activation verbs stay unsupported; no integrated apps are claimed tested. Checked the proposed CGEventTap in [research 06](../research/06-capture-macos.md) and richer action assumptions in [research 09](../research/09-pattern-engine.md). §6.2 requires two target tasks plus negative controls using allowed signals before mining; metadata matches can only ask “Similar app sequence; teach it.” No collection expansion to rescue precision. |
+| **8a. First personal value needs a full setup clock and failure paths** | Accepted | §§1.4, 2.2 and 9.3 distinguish bundled-sample completion from a personal second-input run; time from first launch, separately record installation and prerequisite work, retain failures/abandonments, and split existing-key/dependency versus fresh-account cohorts. Adds missing/unsupported Muse, failed download, fingerprint/signature mismatch, updater removal and unavailable-profile states with draft preservation and validated direct fallback. No claim that account setup is proven to fit thirty minutes. |
+| **8b. Builder/navigation are developer-first** | Accepted | §§2.1–2.6 lead with Tools/Create/Describe, hide inactive Discoveries and deferred Show, and replace the transcript-dominant wireframe with Result → Rules → Examples checked → Access → Save tool. Transcript/source/diffs/usage are advanced details; terminal is deferred. Task-summary wording and example date questions replace default schema/permission-signature vocabulary. |
+| **9a. Monthly arithmetic is correct and should stay** | Accepted | §9.1 preserves $10.69 private workload, $1.02 discovery, $11.71 combined and $14.63 reserve; these are unmeasured assumptions, not typical observed spend or a hard provider cap. Checked [research 15](../research/15-cost-evals.md) and recomputed the selected workload. CLI/tool fees, signing, Windows testing and support stay separate. |
+| **9b. $50 evaluation funding cannot cover the stated denominator** | Accepted | §9.3 separates deterministic regressions from fresh paid evals; calculates 90 builds/contracts = $109.44, forty repair faults = $19.20, twenty healthy controls = $9.60, total baseline $138.24 / reserve $172.80. Proposes ~$137 build-only or $175 combined funding, with $50 per batch and one frozen policy/manifest across batches. Actual retries/children can need more; missing denominators remain incomplete. M0's $10 allowance is separate, and no spend is authorized by this edit. |
+| **9c. Repair production ceiling conflicts with eval p90** | Accepted | §§7.4, 9.1 and 9.3 align at $0.75 total per repair job across at most two candidates, including eval; budget-exhausted attempts count as failures. Removed the $1.50 passing p90. Explicitly raised continuation is a separate reported policy cohort, not a silent ceiling change. Repair itself is deferred. |
+| **10a. Windows MSIX/runtime delivery chain is not established** | Accepted | §5.4 adds the pre-schedule packaged vertical spike: Tauri → MSIX identity/activation → OCR → selected WGC → bounded UIA → external Muse/API auth or direct fallback → separate AppContainer Deno → broker pipe → update. Records manifest, trust levels, token/SID/capabilities/ACLs and denial evidence. Tauri's documented MSI/NSIS routes do not make MSIX a bundle switch; package identity is not worker confinement. Checked [research 07](../research/07-capture-windows.md), [Tauri installers](https://v2.tauri.app/distribute/windows-installer/) and [Microsoft AppContainer launch](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/secauthz/implementing-an-appcontainer). M6/M7 dates await the funded spike and physical tester. |
+| **10b. Windows Muse availability/UAC and Mac picker distinctions** | Accepted | §5.4 keeps documented Windows Muse support and distinguishes possible one-time sandbox setup UAC from an elevated observer/security bypass; the latter remains prohibited. §5.2 requires picker-only versus broad Screen Recording, helper attribution, revoke/relaunch and signed-update tests on each claimed Mac OS. Docs do not establish actual integration. Confirmed [Muse platform differences](https://dev.meta.ai/docs/muse-code); checked picker concerns against [research 06](../research/06-capture-macos.md). |
+| **Additional spike blockers and feasible exit evidence** | Accepted | §10 now orders secure harness/profile/confinement decisions before paid use, then runtime admission before SDK, trusted staged CSV before generated output, and separate timeboxed synthetic capture. M0 lists exact artifacts/statuses, missing-key/signing/budget prerequisites and independent personal-login health. Full updater, six families, general repair, release-scale evaluation and matured retention are excluded from its exit criterion. Historical account scenario stays prohibited; no credential repair is attempted. |
+| **Additional proposed thirty-minute journey and usability test** | Accepted | §2.2 retains the review's concrete 0–3/3–8/8–13/13–18/18–25/25–30 minute outcomes as unmeasured targets. Adds five unfamiliar-user formative gate, ≥2 non-developers, ≥4 second-input completions with prerequisites, all understanding cloud/read/write scope and stopping active build, zero accidental grants, and bad-column/denied-Show recovery. §1.1 compares total effort with an existing agent. |
+| **Additional trust/consent details** | Accepted | §§2.2, 2.6–2.7 and 7.4 explain real-desktop demonstration effects/disposable samples, confidentiality of schema/filenames/rules even in structural packets, cancellation charges/provider retention, and that three clean runs only reduce navigation within enforced scope. Every new MVP input still stages and approves its exact output. |
